<section id="S4.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">4.2 </span>Performance Comparison</h3>

<div id="S4.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This work introduces the Multi-Agent Scalable Transformer (MAST), marking the first scalable multi-agent environment for audio-visual embodied navigation in 3D spaces. To demonstrate the effectiveness of MAST, we compare it with prior single-agent audio-visual navigation baselines, including those by Chen et al. <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib3" title="" class="ltx_ref">3</a>, <a href="#bib.bib4" title="" class="ltx_ref">4</a>]</cite>, Gan et al. <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib10" title="" class="ltx_ref">10</a>]</cite>, and Chen et al. <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib8" title="" class="ltx_ref">8</a>]</cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">On the Replica <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib16" title="" class="ltx_ref">16</a>]</cite> dataset, as shown in Table <a href="#S4.T1" title="Table 1 ‣ Evaluation Metrics ‣ 4.1 Experimental Setup ‣ 4 Experiment ‣ Advancing Audio-Visual Navigation Through Multi-Agent Collaboration in 3D Environments" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, quantitative comparisons reveal that our MAST-AVN model outperforms previous single-agent methods across all metrics, both in ‘Heard’ and ‘Unheard’ scenarios. Specifically, MAST-AVN surpasses ORAN <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib8" title="" class="ltx_ref">8</a>]</cite> by 14.5 in SNA<span id="S4.SS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">@</span>Heard, 3.2 in SR<span id="S4.SS2.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">@</span>Heard, 14.9 in SPL<span id="S4.SS2.p2.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">@</span>Heard, 7.3 in SNA<span id="S4.SS2.p2.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">@</span>Unheard, 11.5 in SR<span id="S4.SS2.p2.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">@</span>Unheard, and 12.6 in SPL<span id="S4.SS2.p2.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">@</span>Unheard. Furthermore, our model achieves significant performance improvements compared to AV-WaN <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib4" title="" class="ltx_ref">4</a>]</cite>, the current state-of-the-art waypoint-based baseline. These results underscore the advantages of dual-agent systems in audio-visual navigation and highlight the superiority of our approach over advanced baselines.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Additionally, Table <a href="#S4.T2" title="Table 2 ‣ Evaluation Metrics ‣ 4.1 Experimental Setup ‣ 4 Experiment ‣ Advancing Audio-Visual Navigation Through Multi-Agent Collaboration in 3D Environments" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> showcases notable enhancements on the Matterport3D <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib2" title="" class="ltx_ref">2</a>]</cite> benchmark. Compared to AV-WaN <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib4" title="" class="ltx_ref">4</a>]</cite>, our model achieves gains of 19.0 in SNA<span id="S4.SS2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">@</span>Heard, 5.3 in SR<span id="S4.SS2.p3.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">@</span>Heard, 19.3 in SPL<span id="S4.SS2.p3.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">@</span>Heard, 17.9 in SNA<span id="S4.SS2.p3.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">@</span>Unheard, 16.5 in SR<span id="S4.SS2.p3.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">@</span>Unheard, and 23.8 in SPL<span id="S4.SS2.p3.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">@</span>Unheard. We also observe strong performance against AV-Nav <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib3" title="" class="ltx_ref">3</a>]</cite>, a deep reinforcement learning network based on separate audio-visual encoders. These findings demonstrate the efficacy of MAST in multimodal information fusion and implicit multi-agent interaction.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S4.T3" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 3: </span>Comparison of different Dual-Agent Navigation methods on Replica.</figcaption>
<table id="S4.T3.1" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<thead class="ltx_thead">
<tr id="S4.T3.1.1" class="ltx_tr">
